            <div xml:id="d136-a1-a18">

                <pb facs="0477" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/>


                <head>Republican Army–Headquarters of the commanding general–Number 2.</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Citizen Minister</hi>: I have the honor to inform you
                    that this city was occupied to-day by our forces, driving out 100 traitors that
                    held it, five of whom we killed, wounded 12, and took 59 prisoners, including
                    two principal chiefs, who are dangerously wounded. All the enemy’s horses, arms,
                    equipments, and ammunition were taken.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to make this known to the President, and accept for yourself the
                    assurances of my consideration and obedience.</p>
                <p>Independence and liberty! Nazas, August 8,1866.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FRANCISCO O. ARCE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Citizen <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister of War</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">at Chihuahua</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
